From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:53:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: open a sub-thread from a selection in an agent message
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Following up on one point of a long agent reply meant either asking in
the same thread, where it derails the conversation, or opening a new
thread by hand and pasting the excerpt, where the agent has lost every
bit of context. This patch adds both kinds of sub-thread to the context
menu of an agent message with text selected in it: story 039,
2026-10-22. Zed at the packaged commit has the protocol types for
session/fork but no client call, so the patch also adds fork support to
the agent connection, built so a later devtools sub-thread can reuse it.

What it does. With text selected in an agent message, its context menu
gains, after a separator, "Clean sub-thread" -- a new thread with the
same agent in the same project, nothing inherited -- and "Sub-thread with
context", which forks the agent session through ACP session/fork, so the
new thread's agent knows the whole conversation so far. Both open the
new thread focused with the excerpt in its composer as a Markdown quote
followed by an empty line, and send nothing; the parent thread is left
as it was. "Sub-thread with context" is offered only when the agent
advertises session fork and also supports session load or resume (the
panel could not open the forked session otherwise), and is disabled with
"Wait for the turn to end" while the parent's turn runs. No entry
appears without a selection, on a user message, a thinking block or a
tool call, or in a subagent's thread view (operator decision 2026-10-22:
a fork there would inherit the subagent's conversation while the link
and the header name the root thread). The existing entries are kept.

The new thread is linked to its parent in 0048's organization store
(set_parent, fork kind clean or with_context), shows a "Sub-thread of:
<parent title>" header above its messages whose title opens the parent
("Sub-thread of a deleted thread", not clickable, once the parent is
gone), and, for a fork, a band "Inherited N messages from <title>" (N =
the parent's user and agent messages at the fork; "Inherited the
conversation of <title>" when N is unknown). Its threads-sidebar row
carries a "↳" marker (IconName::ArrowDownRight, the closest existing
glyph) through 0068's ThreadItem::badge, tooltip "Sub-thread of <parent
title>", in every window, kept across a restart. A fork's link is
recorded as soon as it opens; a clean sub-thread's on its first send, so
a clean draft discarded or emptied before that records none. A fork
keeps the parent's thread configuration -- the mode and config option
values 0036 recorded for the parent session are applied to the fork, not
the agent entry's defaults, and written under the fork's id so it
reopens with them; with no record the fork gets the entry's defaults, as
the parent did at its creation (operator decision 2026-10-21).

Protocol status. session/fork is still unstable_ in ACP
(agent-client-protocol 3.4.0, schema 1.12.0, feature
unstable_session_fork, compiled through the workspace's existing
"unstable" feature): a schema bump may rename the types or move the
capability, so re-check on every Zed or adapter bump -- the entry
disappears when an agent stops advertising sessionCapabilities.fork.
Only the ACP v1 connection implements it. That reaches Claude Agent
(Plus), whose unstable_forkSession resumes the SDK session with
forkSession: true and replays no history: the adapter answers
protocolVersion 1, so 0001's v2-first attempt falls back to v1. The v2
connection, the native agent and the test fakes keep the trait default,
which refuses; an adapter that moves to v2 loses the entry until a v2
fork exists.

How. crates/acp_thread/src/connection.rs: AgentConnection gains
supports_fork_session and fork_session, defaulting to "not supported"
exactly as session close does, and StubAgentConnection an opt-in
with_fork_support builder. crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs: an
AcpThread forked_from field, and is_draft_thread is false for a fork
with no entries yet -- its session id is the agent's, fixed at the fork,
so the metadata store keeps it and 0048's admit accepts the link.
crates/agent_servers/src/acp/v1.rs: agent_supports_session_fork,
SessionDirectories::into_fork_session_request (the parent thread's work
directories and the project's MCP servers), and fork_session, which
registers the forked session's AcpThread through register_answered_session
-- new_session's post-response steps, moved into a helper both share --
and closes the fork when the caller is gone before the answer and the
agent supports close. crates/agent_ui/src/sub_thread.rs (new, with
sub_thread/forked_sub_thread.rs and sub_thread/message_menu.rs):
AgentPanel::open_sub_thread(SubThreadRequest, focus), which takes a plain
request rather than a ThreadView so a devtools sub-thread can call it;
the clean path is 0045's new_thread_with_prefilled_prompt, the fork path
opens the registered thread through
create_agent_thread_with_server_for_external_session, so no session/load
is sent and the view starts empty, and holds the forked AcpThread until
the view's first RootThreadUpdated. conversation_view/sub_thread_header.rs
(new) draws the header, the band and the never-used-fork state below.
crates/sidebar/src/sub_thread_marker.rs (new) is the marker.

Failure. A refused or failed fork -- an agent error, no working
directories, no connection -- opens nothing, records no link, toasts
"Couldn't create the sub-thread" and logs a warning with the parent
session id and the agent's error code (code=none for a non-agent
failure). A clean sub-thread whose agent is gone shows 0045's toast. A
refused link keeps the thread open and logs both thread ids and the
store's refusal. Reopening a fork that was never used, which the adapter
answers -32002 (resource not found), keeps the row, the link and the
header and shows "This sub-thread was never used and can't be reopened"
instead of the generic load error. Every log line carries
zeo_sub_thread event=<created|link_failed|open_failed|...> with ids,
kinds and the excerpt's length only, never the excerpt or a title.

Upstream touch points, hooks only. thread_view.rs (+20/-2):
render_message_context_menu's offers_sub_threads flag, fed by 0045's
offers_slash_commands at the agent-chunk call site and false at the
thinking header, the menu_entries call, the header slot in render, and
0045's button closure passing focus. conversation_view.rs (+19/-4): the
mod line, the sub_thread view state, the store observation, and the
SubThreadUnavailable server state's arms. agent_panel.rs (+33/-7):
0045's new_thread_with_prefilled_prompt takes focus and returns the
opened conversation; pub(crate) panel_workspace, show_agent_thread,
has_open_project and create_agent_thread_with_server_for_external_session;
one line in ensure_draft's reuse branch drops the pending link of an
emptied clean draft. agent_servers/src/acp.rs: 0036's ConfigRecorder
waits for the fork's inherited write before its first snapshot.
agent_panel/tests (0045's): the new focus argument. agent_ui.rs and
sidebar.rs: module lines, and in sidebar.rs one render_thread line
between the project-name label and 0068's tag chips. No Cargo.toml, no
Cargo.lock, no new crate or feature.

Tests: 89 -- 87 in twelve new test files, acp_thread
connection/fork_tests.rs (10); agent_servers acp/v1/fork_session_tests.rs
(6) and fork_config_tests.rs (6); agent_ui sub_thread_tests/ pure (10),
clean (11), fork (9), fork_abandoned (3), menu (8), menu_subagent (2),
header (10), reopen (4), with support.rs; sidebar
sidebar_sub_thread_tests.rs (8) -- and 2 in the test module of the new
agent_ui conversation_view/sub_thread_header.rs.

Group claude-agent-acp-plus, last of it: it calls 0045's
new_thread_with_prefilled_prompt and extends 0036's config recorder, and
the only agent that advertises fork today is the Plus adapter. It needs
0048's store and 0068's ThreadItem::badge, both ungrouped. 0052, 0057,
0058, 0063 and 0067 are regenerated on top with offsets, index lines and
context only; 0063's devtools badge now sits before this patch's marker
line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
